      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — fixing argument order in assertions, removing unused imports, and adding clarifying comments.The improved test compiles successfully. The changes made were: removed unused imports, extracted `alwaysEncodeChars` into a named variable, renamed intermediate variables to be more descriptive (`encodedString`, `decodedString`), fixed the `assertEquals` argument order in the decode assertion to follow JUnit convention (expected first, actual second), and added a Javadoc comment explaining the encoding rules so readers immediately understand why each portion of the input is encoded the way it is."
